    "Ordinary latest SDK repeats the old small allocated-arena tail growth while FDs/threads remain constant.",
    "Map-only without detection/segmentation/BPU reproduces~1.5KiB/lifecycle allocated growth; detseg-only tail is almost flat. Map rendering is sufficient for the differential.",
    "Scratch-buffer-only attempt does not remove the growth; it is not the fix and has no measured wall-time benefit.",
    "Exact-board-linked traces locate three224/64/504B blocks in OpenCV TraceManager TLS first touched by renderOriginalMap cv::resize parallel_for. Exact disassembly confirms terminated-thread data pushed to an accumulator rather than deleted.",
    "Each100x10 lifecycle retains two touched-worker copies;100x1 retains one. It scales with newly touched worker threads, not simply with frames.",
    "Targeted serial resize+RGB exchange preserves pixels and removes the OpenCV parallel tracing entry path without global thread/TLS changes.",
    "Final minimal44cdd0 ordinary300 has last25sample uord delta0B and last50+64B vs baseline+35696B/+74160B. After_destroy threads remain18/FD13. Final100x1 trace has no OpenCV group at20/21/50/100, only unrelatedlibdnn1039requestedB at100.",
    "Large RSS variation remains substantially allocator free-page retention. No inference from RSS alone to unreachable objects, and no blanket third-party leak-free statement."
  ],
